# Windows launcher scripts must keep CRLF endings.
#
# cmd.exe seeks by byte offset through a running .bat file, and LF-only line
# endings can leave it mis-positioned around labels and goto - which is exactly
# the machinery UPDATE MIRAGE.bat relies on. Git normalising these to LF on
# checkout would break them on the one platform they exist for.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Everything else: leave as-is rather than guess.
* -text
